     "title": "Step 3",
     "description": "CP-6 is combined with tetrahydrofuran, sodium carbonate, and ethyl chloroformate, then heated to reflux. Upon reaction completion, the mixture is filtered and quenched with sodium hydroxide, n-hexane is added, the layers are separated, and the organic layer is distilled with ethanol and stirred with water (CPP #3.1). After filtering and drying it results in CP-7.",
     "code": {
      "text": "Chemical synthesis step"
