     "title": "Step 4",
     "description": "CP-7 and CP-8 are combined in methylene chloride followed by the addition of tetra-n-butylammonium bromide and aqueous sodium hydroxide solution while mixing. Upon reaction completion, methylene chloride and water are added (CPP #4.1); ethanol content is monitored by IPC #1. The mixture is separated, washed, cooled (CPP #4.2, IPC #2) and concentrated with ethanol. After filtering and drying it results in CP-9 (Sakuramil).",
     "code": {
      "text": "Chemical synthesis step"
     },
